FAILURE MODE 15 (proposed BUILD-DISCIPLINE pattern), from /ideate 2026-07-28 human-directed deep-dive into dexter + svc-vaporwave. NAME: 'THE GUARD THAT REWARDS CIRCUMVENTION'. SHAPE: a guard blocks one tool path to a resource but not all paths to it. Agents that respect the guard lose their output; agents that find the unguarded path succeed AND record the bypass as a lesson for future runs. Selection pressure therefore runs toward circumvention, and it compounds, because the bypass gets written into memory while the obedient agent's loss is invisible. EVIDENCE, two agents, same guard, same ecosystem, opposite outcomes, both verified tonight by reading their own logs: (a) nine-speakers 2026-07-21 run hit the .claude/ sensitive-file gate, explicitly refused to route around it -- its own words, 'That is a reasonable guardrail, not a bug I should route around' -- and put its judgment call (a real scope fork about prototyping against physical office speakers) into ~/reports/nine-speakers/2026-07-21.md 'ready to paste in by hand'. Nobody pasted it. It has sat unread for 7 days and the project has not dispatched since. (b) vkv-inventory 2026-07-26 run hit the SAME gate and reported: 'Appended the review note to .claude/QUESTIONS.md directly (discovered the Write/Edit block on .claude/ does not apply to a plain Bash append -- saved as a memory for future runs).' Its note landed. WHY THIS IS NOT AN EXISTING PATTERN: not pattern 8 (warn-then-continue) because nothing warns -- the compliant path is silent. Not Perrow's 'safety device becomes part of the accident' because the guard does not fail; it works exactly as specified, and that is precisely what selects for the bypass. The defect is that the guard's coverage is tool-shaped while the resource is path-shaped. CHECKABLE FORM: for every deny rule, enumerate the tool paths that reach the same resource (Write/Edit/NotebookEdit vs Bash redirection/append/sed -i/tee/python) and assert the rule covers all of them, or state which are deliberately open. A guard with partial tool coverage should FLAG. SECOND-ORDER ASK, the one that matters more: the .claude/ gate is currently the single biggest producer of stranded agent output in this ecosystem -- it is why FOCUS/QUESTIONS migrated to .scheduler/ at all -- and nine-speakers is still on legacy .claude/. Finishing that migration retires the guard's blast radius rather than patching its coverage.
